<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>Library ebooks are the best deal in reading: free, legal, and delivered as open EPUB files. The device landscape has never been more varied — Kindle keeps its US-only integration and a hack that may be cracking, Kobo and PocketBook offer native support, Android e-ink devices read Libby in an app, and Xteink owners just gained a path via CrossPoint Reader's Protected Content plug-in.</p>

<p>Whichever device you own, the universal EPUB workflow is your safety net: borrow in Libby, unlock with Adobe Digital Editions or Calibre, convert to fit your reader, and read. Library books are EPUB books, and once you know that, no e-reader is locked out of your local library again.</p>
